# The scenario editor's waypoint keys, each on the cell selected before it:
# Alt and a letter names the cell as that waypoint, Shift-Home moves the home
# cell there, Shift-R the reinforcement cell, the full stop asks for a
# two-letter waypoint name in an edit box, and Alt-Space takes a waypoint off
# its cell.
#
# The map takes a button that is down when it looks, so selecting a cell
# holds it for a few frames.
# args: -EDITOR
at 201 press 250 120
at 204 release 250 120
at 220 keydown ALT
at 221 key C
at 225 keyup ALT
at 260 shot waypoint_c
at 261 press 420 120
at 264 release 420 120
at 270 keydown SHIFT
at 271 key HOME
at 275 keyup SHIFT
at 300 shot home_moved
at 301 press 250 200
at 304 release 250 200
at 310 keydown SHIFT
at 311 key R
at 315 keyup SHIFT
at 340 shot reinforcement_moved
at 341 press 420 200
at 344 release 420 200
at 350 key PERIOD
at 380 shot name_box
at 381 type BD
at 385 key BACKSPACE
at 389 type F
at 400 shot name_typed
# Return does nothing while the edit box has the keys; OK it is.
at 401 key RETURN
at 420 click 136 116
at 460 shot waypoint_bf
at 461 press 250 120
at 464 release 250 120
at 470 keydown ALT
at 471 key SPACE
at 475 keyup ALT
at 500 shot waypoint_c_removed
at 501 quit
